WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.509 --> 00:00:05.176
- [Narrator] This is
the bald uakari monkey.

00:00:08.945 --> 00:00:12.058
These monkeys are mostly known
for their bright red faces,

00:00:12.058 --> 00:00:14.442
which are an indicator of good health.

00:00:14.442 --> 00:00:17.815
Sick monkeys develop pale faces.

00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:21.428
Unlike most primates, bald
uakaris have very short tails

00:00:21.428 --> 00:00:22.678
and long coats.

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:26.183
The uakari is an arboreal primate,

00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:28.440
which means they live in the treetops,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.710
mostly because of forest
flooding in the rainy season.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.982
During the dry season,

00:00:32.982 --> 00:00:37.247
they return to the
ground to look for seeds.

00:00:37.247 --> 00:00:39.879
The bald uakari are native
to the western Amazon

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:44.524
of Brazil and Peru and are
considered a vulnerable species.

00:00:44.524 --> 00:00:46.293
Female uakaris can only give birth

00:00:46.293 --> 00:00:48.645
to a single infant every two years,

00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:51.366
so the population can't grow rapidly.

00:00:51.366 --> 00:00:53.951
These primates are threatened
primarily by hunting

00:00:53.951 --> 00:00:58.942
and destruction of their
habitat, mostly by deforestation.

00:00:58.942 --> 00:01:01.525
This is the bald uakari monkey.

